  "proof": "Source: parent proof Step 4 (Simon (4), chapter-03.txt lines 637-645), with ρ − 1/k replaced by an arbitrary s ∈ (0, ρ). Notation: r(y) := |y − x|, B_t := B_t(x), B̄_t := closed ball, Dζ(y) := fderiv ℝ ζ y, L^N = volume.\n\n1. (Definition and Lipschitz bound.) Let ζ(y) := min{1, max{0, (ρ − r(y))/(ρ − s)}}. The function r is 1-Lipschitz, t ↦ (ρ − t)/(ρ − s) is (ρ − s)⁻¹-Lipschitz and t ↦ min{1, max{0, t}} is 1-Lipschitz, so ζ is (ρ − s)⁻¹-Lipschitz; take K := (ρ − s)⁻¹ ∈ ℝ≥0.\n\n2. (Values and support.) 0 ≤ ζ ≤ 1. If r(y) < s then (ρ − r(y))/(ρ − s) > 1, so ζ(y) = 1; thus ζ = 1 on B_s. If r(y) ≥ ρ then ρ − r(y) ≤ 0, so ζ(y) = 0; thus ζ = 0 outside B_ρ. Hence support ζ ⊆ B_ρ, tsupport ζ ⊆ closure(B_ρ) ⊆ B̄_ρ (a closed set), and since B̄_ρ is compact (ℝ^N is proper), ζ has compact support.\n\n3. (The derivative.) Consider the open sets I := B_s = {r < s}, O := {r > ρ} and A := {s < r < ρ}. On I, ζ ≡ 1, and on O, ζ ≡ 0, so Dζ = 0 on I ∪ O (ζ is locally constant there). For y ∈ A, (ρ − r(y))/(ρ − s) ∈ (0, 1), so on the open set A, ζ coincides with y ↦ (ρ − r(y))/(ρ − s). As y ≠ x on A (r(y) > s > 0), r is differentiable at y with Dr(y)h = ⟨(y − x)/|y − x|, h⟩, hence Dζ(y) = −(ρ − s)⁻¹ ⟨(y − x)/|y − x|, ·⟩, whose operator norm is (ρ − s)⁻¹ (the functional h ↦ ⟨u, h⟩ has norm |u| = 1). The remaining set ℝ^N ∖ (I ∪ O ∪ A) = {r = s} ∪ {r = ρ} consists of two spheres of positive radius; for N ≥ 1 they are L^N-null (Mathlib Measure.addHaar_sphere), and for N = 0 they are empty (the only point of ℝ^0 is x, where r = 0). Therefore |Dζ| = (ρ − s)⁻¹ 1_A holds L^N-a.e.\n\n4. (The integral identity.) Let G be L^N-null-measurable. By step 3, ∫_G |Dζ| dL^N = (ρ − s)⁻¹ L^N(G ∩ A).toReal: the integrand agrees L^N-a.e. (hence a.e. for L^N restricted to G) with the constant (ρ − s)⁻¹ times the indicator of the measurable set A, and L^N(G ∩ A) ≤ L^N(B_ρ) < ∞. The ball B_ρ is the disjoint union of the measurable sets B_s, {r = s} and A, so L^N(G ∩ B_ρ) = L^N(G ∩ B_s) + L^N(G ∩ {r = s}) + L^N(G ∩ A) = L^N(G ∩ B_s) + L^N(G ∩ A), because the middle term is ≤ L^N({r = s}) = 0. All these quantities are finite (≤ L^N(B_ρ) < ∞), so L^N(G ∩ A).toReal = L^N(G ∩ B_ρ).toReal − L^N(G ∩ B_s).toReal, and therefore ∫_G |Dζ| dL^N = (L^N(G ∩ B_ρ).toReal − L^N(G ∩ B_s).toReal)/(ρ − s). ∎",
  "key_steps": [
    "ζ(y) := min{1, max{0, (ρ − |y − x|)/(ρ − s)}} is (ρ − s)⁻¹-Lipschitz, takes values in [0, 1], equals 1 on B_s(x) and 0 off B_ρ(x), and has tsupport ⊆ B̄_ρ(x) (compact).",
    "Dζ = 0 on the open sets B_s(x) and {|y − x| > ρ}; on the open annulus A, Dζ(y) = −(ρ − s)⁻¹⟨(y − x)/|y − x|, ·⟩ has norm (ρ − s)⁻¹; the two spheres are L^N-null (or empty if N = 0).",
    "∫_G|Dζ| = (ρ − s)⁻¹L^N(G ∩ A), and L^N(G ∩ B_ρ) = L^N(G ∩ B_s) + L^N(G ∩ A) by disjoint additivity, all terms finite."
  ],
